message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "TDMM: Bayesian Time-Dynamic Models with Optional Mixed Effects"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Grigsby
    given-names: Makena
  - family-names: Kürüm
    given-names: Esra
version: 0.3.0
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23742177
date-released: 2026-10-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/esrakurum/Bayesian-TDMM"
abstract: "TDMM provides Bayesian time-dynamic models with optional mixed effects for Gaussian, Bernoulli, and Poisson outcomes. Coefficients vary smoothly over time. A subject-specific random intercept supports repeated observations; without it, the model supports independent observations. In the independent setting, time may represent age, time since an event, or time relative to an event."
keywords:
  - Bayesian modeling
  - longitudinal data
  - time-varying coefficients
  - mixed-effects models
  - P-splines
  - JAGS
